{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"Sessions","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"Sessions","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" to its session’s identifier. A session goes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The enricher tracks ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","type":"reference"},{"text":" before each session’s first event, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has no ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","type":"reference"},{"text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, by the record’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s enrichers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StandardContext"},{"type":"text","text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LifecycleTracking"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationOpened"},{"type":"text","text":" after a long time in the background starts a new session here, though"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither module knows about the other."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Sessions","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [try .sessions(timeout: .seconds(15 * 60), kinds: [.started])])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))  \/\/ tracks SessionStarted, then SignedUp, both with the sam